
1. University match — requirements, cost, country, field
  ✓ unrecorded IELTS/SAT scores do not lower fit
  ✓ fit score carries no Reach/Match/Safety admissions category
  ✓ unrecorded IELTS is not treated as a failed requirement
  ✓ unrecorded SAT is not treated as a failed requirement
  ✓ field alignment is the top reason (weight 12)
  ✓ what-if values recompute against an immutable in-memory profile copy
  ✓ what-if can explicitly return unknown values to null without writing the source profile
  ✓ family income does not replace a missing explicit annual budget
  ✓ fit explanations never score household income as available funding
  ✓ strong profile → high score
  ✓ max 2 reasons
  ✓ max 2 issues
  ✓ activities, work years, and publications do not inflate university fit
  ✓ university fit does not claim activities strengthen admission
  ✓ IELTS exactly at the bar → no IELTS issue
  ✓ IELTS below the bar → penalty vs a score that meets it
  ✓ IELTS below → issue asks the student to verify the programme-level policy
  ✓ no published minimums → no test issues
  ✓ no published minimums → high score
  ✓ TOEFL instead of IELTS adds an informational signal without changing fit or claiming equivalence
  ✓ Duolingo is surfaced as recorded context, never converted to IELTS
  ✓ unrelated field → visible issue when requirements are met
  ✓ unrelated field → lower score than a matching field
  ✓ unknown target major → no field claim either way
  ✓ unscaled GPA > 4 → no GPA comparison (no false 'well above')

2. subjectAlignment / majorOverlap — word-based, blank-safe
  ✓ exact field → strong
  ✗ superset field → strong
  ✓ unrelated field → none
  ✓ blank student major → unknown
  ✓ blank program focus → unknown
  ✓ 'AI' does NOT match 'Sustainable Engineering'
  ✗ 'AI' matches 'AI & Data Science'
  ✓ short tokens are kept by the tokenizer
  ✓ stop words are dropped
  ✓ no comparable words → null, not a fake 0.5

3. Scholarship match — level aliases, majors, English tests
  ✓ 'Master''s' profile matches a ['Master','PhD'] award
  ✓ 'Master''s' is NOT reported as 'Only open to'
  ✓ PhD profile matches a ['Master','PhD'] award
  ✓ Bachelor profile → explicit mismatch issue
  ✓ Bachelor profile → lower score than a matching level
  ✓ missing profile level → unknown (no mismatch claim)
  ✓ Cyrillic 'магистратура' matches 'Master'
  ✓ blank target major → NO 'your field is eligible' claim
  ✓ blank target major → asks the student to add it
  ✓ 'AI' is not reported eligible for an Engineering/Public Health award
  ✓ 'Computer Science' matches a Computer Science award
  ✓ 'All' majors award → no field issue for a blank major
  ✓ no English test is not scored as a scholarship failure
  ✓ TOEFL instead of IELTS adds a non-penalizing scholarship signal
  ✓ merit-based + strong GPA → reason
  ✓ merit-based + incomparable GPA → no invented merit reason

4. Shared helpers — GPA scale and degree levels
  ✓ 4.0 scale keeps the value
  ✓ 100-point scale converts proportionally
  ✓ 5-point scale converts proportionally
  ✓ no scale, value ≤ 4 → unknown
  ✓ no scale, value > 4 → unknown (never 4.0)
  ✓ explicit zero GPA is valid; negative GPA is unknown
  ✓ alias: Master's ↔ Master
  ✓ alias: MSc ↔ Master
  ✓ alias: Bachelor vs Master-only → mismatch
  ✓ 'All' catalogue level matches anything
  ✓ unknown profile level → unknown
  ✓ unknown catalogue level → unknown
  ✓ unknown is never coerced to All
  ✓ multi-level label is recognised
  ✓ a label with an unrecognised part stays unspecified
  ✓ JSON-array label is compared, not read as unknown

5. SAT/ACT catalogue figures are compared only for undergraduate applicants
  ✓ graduate applicant at a graduate-only university → no SAT issue
  ✓ a stored undergraduate SAT bar does not move a graduate applicant's score
  ✓ undergraduate applicant's missing SAT remains unknown, not a failure
  ✓ a graduate applicant at an undergraduate+graduate university is not scored on SAT
  ✓ unknown level still shows the published SAT bar (never hidden)
  ✓ graduate-only institution → test does not apply
  ✓ undergraduate institution + undergraduate student → applies
  ✓ unknown institution level keeps the published bar
  ✓ hasUndergraduateAdmission: All → true
  ✓ hasUndergraduateAdmission: Master only → false
  ✓ hasUndergraduateAdmission: unknown → false (never claimed)
  ✓ a Master programme ignores a stray SAT minimum
  ✓ a Bachelor programme still assesses the SAT minimum

6. Precision — continuous grading and visible arithmetic
  ✓ the breakdown components sum to the raw score
  ✓ the displayed score is the raw score rounded once
  ✓ every dimension is reported, with the unmeasured ones marked not-compared
  ✓ evidence coverage and level are derived from measured dimensions, not fit score
  ✓ zero available dimensions stay limited evidence, never a probability
  ✓ a dimension with no data contributes exactly 0
  ✓ the GPA reason carries the exact points it contributed
  ✓ GPA 3.80 against a 3.50 bar earns the graded 9.0, not a flat 10
  ✓ meeting a minimum exactly is neutral (0), not a bonus
  ✓ GPA grading has no cliff (max 1 point per 0.01)
  ✓ a better GPA never scores lower
  ✓ a larger budget never scores lower
  ✓ non-USD canonical costs never fall back to stale USD mirrors
  ✓ missing living cost is unknown, not treated as zero
  ✓ a small budget gap costs far less than a large one
  ✓ both gaps are still penalties, never awards
  ✓ a 0.5-band margin over the IELTS bar scores strictly higher than an exact pass
  ✓ scholarship breakdown also adds up to its raw score
  ✓ a higher GPA never lowers a scholarship score

